### Product Service (READ SIDE) - example requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### This service only READS. Writes: product-write-service (port 8089) or POST/PUT/DELETE via the gateway.
### Data arrives from MySQL through Debezium. Counts assume the 30 sample products.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products

### 1. Health - expect "status":"UP" (elasticsearch UP)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### 2. Default listing - newest first
GET {{api}}

> {%
    client.global.set("firstProductId", response.body.content[0].id);
%}

### 3. Get by id - expect a UUID id and a "version" field
GET {{api}}/{{firstProductId}}

### 4. Laptops under $1,000, cheapest first - 7 products
GET {{api}}?category=laptop&maxPrice=1000&sortBy=price

### 5. Apple products - 8 products
GET {{api}}?brand=apple

### 6. Exactly 16 GB RAM - 9 products
GET {{api}}?minRamGb=16&maxRamGb=16

### 7. Text search with typo tolerance
GET {{api}}?q=gamng

### 8. Next page
GET {{api}}?q=gaming&size=3&page=1

### 9. Facets
GET {{api}}/facets

### 10. Writes are no longer served here - expect 405 Method Not Allowed
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "X-1" }

### 11. Unknown id - expect 404
GET {{api}}/does-not-exist
